# K03 NS-ROLES-2 REQUIRED POSITIVE, red until its dependency is built (Codex K03-NS2-COVERAGE-20261007-21;
# steps/defects.md#reference-field-consumers).
# take(Shell) with Outer's `in: Inner` and Shell's `in: Box`: Box has the x take writes through slot\in, so Shell is
# admitted to (Outer: slot) by the fields its Consumer reads (Box's extra y unread); the write reaches Box.  Today the
# admission through reference fields of two models is not built: "root operation not walkable yet: an admission to a
# Structure type through a Structure field of another type" (unit_s7_nested_missing keeps its refusal with owned
# nested fields).  Exit 7; 81 for a wrong result, 82 if the write did not reach Box.
Inner:
    size_t: x 0U
end: Inner
Box:
    size_t: x 0U
    size_t: y 5U
end: Box
Outer:
    in: Inner
end: Outer
Shell:
    in: Box
end: Shell
fn: take (Outer: slot) int
    slot\in\x: 1U
    return: 4
end: take
fn: m () int
    if: take(Shell) != 4
        return: 81
    if: Box\x != 1U
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
